{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" owns the session server, the capture pipeline and the input lane, and ties them to the helper’s features. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeadwireMac"},{"type":"text","text":" app starts it only while Streaming or Input is on, so a helper used for the display mode alone opens no port."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Listening","type":"heading","anchor":"Listening"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator\/start()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" opens one TLS listener for every transport: the USB cable, the network (Ethernet or Wi-Fi) and Direct wireless. The listener is advertised over Bonjour. Only a device in the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/TrustList","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" gets past the handshake; an unpaired device first pairs through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/PairingService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which judges one pairing request a connection and then closes it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Joining","type":"heading","anchor":"Joining"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a paired device’s session is up, the coordinator records its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/SessionInfo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and sends the device the host’s information, its capabilities and the Mac’s facts: its active keyboard layout and its Mission Control shortcuts, so the device’s Bluetooth path types and gestures the same way when the helper is not running."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session joins in warm standby. The device opens every link it can, so the helper streams nothing until the device asks for video on the link it shows. While any paired device is connected, the capture and the encoder session stay up, so video resumes with one keyframe; with no device connected, the helper captures nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Streaming","type":"heading","anchor":"Streaming"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The device asks for one of three kinds of video:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the full-quality stream."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Standby","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": nothing is sent, and the capture keeps running."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Backup","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": a second, low-rate stream at no more than 30 fps, scaled down on the GPU from the same capture, for switching links without a gap."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every keyframe goes with the HEVC parameter sets. A device with more than two messages it has not taken yet has its next delta dropped and waits for a keyframe, because a queue of frames is latency.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the hardware encoder stops returning frames, the stream moves to the software encoder, and the hardware is tested again while devices stay connected. If the capture stops on its own or the pipeline cannot start, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/StreamHealth","isActive":true},{"text":" rebuilds it after waits of 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 30 seconds, then waits for Try Again in the menu. Screen Recording taken away is not retried; the permission check brings the stream back.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Input","type":"heading","anchor":"Input"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s input goes from the network to the input lane and is posted on ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostInputActor","isActive":true},{"text":"’s own serial queue, in the order the device sent it, without the main actor. Each session has its own ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/InputDeviceID","isActive":true},{"text":", so the buttons and keys one device holds down are released when that device leaves, never when another does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Link health","type":"heading","anchor":"Link-health"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A device pings at least once a second on every link it keeps. After 2 seconds without hearing it, the helper stops sending it video, and resumes from a keyframe once it is heard again. After 30 seconds the session is closed and everything it held is released.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Leaving","type":"heading","anchor":"Leaving"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a session ends, for whatever reason, the coordinator releases what that device held, cancels its calibration, drops its extended display request and refreshes what the pipeline runs for the sessions still open. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator\/stop()","isActive":true},{"text":" stops taking input, releases everything, says goodbye to every device and stops capturing. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator\/unpaired(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" closes every session of a device that was removed from the trust list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/sessionlifecycle"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"A device’s session","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacHost"}]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"What happens on the Mac from the moment a paired device connects until it leaves.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/SessionLifecycle"},"references":{"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/HostCoordinator":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HostCoordinator"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator","title":"HostCoordinator","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/hostcoordinator","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Ties the session server, the capture pipeline and input posting to the helper’s features.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HostCoordinator","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/HostCoordinator/unpaired(_:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Closes every session of an unpaired device."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unpaired"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Data","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4DataV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"unpaired(_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator\/unpaired(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/hostcoordinator\/unpaired(_:)"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/HostInputActor":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/hostinputactor","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HostInputActor","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"HostInputActor","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HostInputActor","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where helper input is posted: one serial queue of its own, never the main actor."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostInputActor"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/HostCoordinator/start()":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Starts listening."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"start"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"start()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator\/start()","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/hostcoordinator\/start()"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/PairingService":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PairingService","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/PairingService","title":"PairingService","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/pairingservice","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pairing window the menu opens, and the answer to each pairing connection."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PairingService","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/StreamHealth":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the stream runs, and when it stopped on its own, how the helper rebuilds it."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StreamHealth","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"StreamHealth","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StreamHealth","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/StreamHealth","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/streamhealth"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/TrustList":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrustList","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/TrustList","title":"TrustList","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/trustlist","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The keys the session protocol admits: every paired device, plus development pins."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrustList","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Headwire Helper’s streaming, input and pairing: the code that serves paired devices from the Mac."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost","title":"HeadwireMacHost","kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/HostCoordinator/stop()":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Stops taking input, releases everything devices hold, says goodbye to them, and stops capturing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stop"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"stop()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator\/stop()","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/hostcoordinator\/stop()"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/InputDeviceID":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/inputdeviceid","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InputDeviceID","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"InputDeviceID","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InputDeviceID","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One connected device’s session, as the input layer tells devices apart."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/InputDeviceID"},"doc://HeadwireMacHost/documentation/HeadwireMacHost/SessionInfo":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremachost\/sessioninfo","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SessionInfo","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SessionInfo","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SessionInfo","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Who a session is, as the helper saw it at the handshake."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/SessionInfo"}}}